    "solution": "Pick up the lantern and let the support settle. While carrying it, briefly hold Down to store a partial load. Release Down and throw Right: the lantern travels into the lower pressure pocket and opens the high landing gate. Step toward the lip and jump from the returning plate. Only enough rise to clear the raised bridge fits beneath the low ceiling teeth; a full held jump from full charge hits them, while an unloaded or very lightly loaded jump falls short. Continue along the upper bridge while the lantern remains below. An accurately shortened jump from a larger charge is also a valid height-control solution.",
