    "revision": {
      "date": "2026-10-09",
      "archive": "scripts/room-bank/archive/run4-before-superrooms/base/35-bank-f35.json",
      "latestChanges": "Restored low ceiling spikes, raised bridge one tile, and rebuilt the intended route around choosing a partial load while carrying the gate weight."
    },
    "userFeedback": {
      "date": "2026-10-09",
      "comment": "Prior full spring jump was trivial; require a precise small spring arc: too high hits ceiling spikes, too little misses the landing."
    },
    "designNotes": "Restored the intended partial spring problem instead of opening the roof. The bridge is one tile higher than the preceding revision, and a long downward spike ceiling leaves a three-tile passage above it. The normal partial-load route has ten consecutive successful manual load durations (9–18 frames), and seven departure step timings (6–12 frames) succeed at the demonstrated 11-frame charge. No dash is available. Full charge with a held jump hits the teeth; near-zero charge and waiting for the spring to settle miss the landing. Variable jump height remains an honest alternate: a precisely shortened jump can tame a larger charge, which still requires choosing the arc rather than taking the automatic full launch. The lantern still separately opens the lower weight gate.",
    "placementNote": "Author placement estimate updated from qualitative user feedback; not a numeric user rating.",
    "reclassifiedFrom": "fractured",
    "reclassificationReason": "User requested Base placement after a precision spring revision; acceptance is revised pending that review.",
